msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4297
msgid "Indentation with the continuation indent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4299
msgid ""
"Fundamentally, C++11 braced lists are formatted exactly like function calls "
"would be formatted in their place. If the braced list follows a name (e.g. a "
"type or variable name), clang-format formats as if the `{}` were the "
"parentheses of a function call with that name. If there is no name, a zero-"
"length name is assumed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4314
msgid ""
"`BLS_AlignFirstComment` (in configuration: `AlignFirstComment`) Same as "
"`FunctionCall`, except for the handling of a comment at the begin, it then "
"aligns everything following with the comment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4318
msgid ""
"No spaces inside the braced list. (Even for a comment at the first position.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4321
msgid ""
"Indentation with the continuation indent, except when followed by a line "
"comment, then it uses the block indent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4337
msgid ""
"**DeriveLineEnding** (`Boolean`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 10` {ref}`¶ "
"<DeriveLineEnding>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4339
msgid ""
"This option is **deprecated**. See `DeriveLF` and `DeriveCRLF` of "
"`LineEnding`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4344
msgid ""
"**DerivePointerAlignment** (`Boolean`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 3.7` {ref}"
"`¶ <DerivePointerAlignment>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4346
msgid ""
"If `true`, analyze the formatted file for the most common alignment of `&` "
"and `*`. Pointer and reference alignment styles are going to be updated "
"according to the preferences found in the file. `PointerAlignment` is then "
"used only as fallback."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4354
msgid ""
"**DisableFormat** (`Boolean`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 3.7` {ref}`¶ "
"<DisableFormat>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4356
msgid "Disables formatting completely."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4360
msgid ""
"**EmptyLineAfterAccessModifier** (`EmptyLineAfterAccessModifierStyle`) "
"{versionbadge}`clang-format 13` {ref}`¶ <EmptyLineAfterAccessModifier>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4362
msgid ""
"Defines when to put an empty line after access modifiers. "
"`EmptyLineBeforeAccessModifier` configuration handles the number of empty "
"lines between two access modifiers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4368
msgid ""
"`ELAAMS_Never` (in configuration: `Never`) Remove all empty lines after "
"access modifiers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4385
msgid ""
"`ELAAMS_Leave` (in configuration: `Leave`) Keep existing empty lines after "
"access modifiers. MaxEmptyLinesToKeep is applied instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4389
msgid ""
"`ELAAMS_Always` (in configuration: `Always`) Always add empty line after "
"access modifiers if there are none. MaxEmptyLinesToKeep is applied also."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4416
msgid ""
"**EmptyLineBeforeAccessModifier** (`EmptyLineBeforeAccessModifierStyle`) "
"{versionbadge}`clang-format 12` {ref}`¶ <EmptyLineBeforeAccessModifier>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4418
msgid "Defines in which cases to put empty line before access modifiers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4422
msgid ""
"`ELBAMS_Never` (in configuration: `Never`) Remove all empty lines before "
"access modifiers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4439
msgid ""
"`ELBAMS_Leave` (in configuration: `Leave`) Keep existing empty lines before "
"access modifiers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4442
msgid ""
"`ELBAMS_LogicalBlock` (in configuration: `LogicalBlock`) Add empty line only "
"when access modifier starts a new logical block. Logical block is a group of "
"one or more member fields or functions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4462
msgid ""
"`ELBAMS_Always` (in configuration: `Always`) Always add empty line before "
"access modifiers unless access modifier is at the start of struct or class "
"definition."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4488
msgid ""
"**EnumTrailingComma** (`EnumTrailingCommaStyle`) {versionbadge}`clang-format "
"21` {ref}`¶ <EnumTrailingComma>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4490
msgid ""
"Insert a comma (if missing) or remove the comma at the end of an `enum` "
"enumerator list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4494
#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6662
msgid ""
"Setting this option to any value other than `Leave` could lead to incorrect "
"code formatting due to clang-format's lack of complete semantic information. "
"As such, extra care should be taken to review code changes made by this "
"option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4502
msgid ""
"`ETC_Leave` (in configuration: `Leave`) Don't insert or remove trailing "
"commas."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4510
msgid "`ETC_Insert` (in configuration: `Insert`) Insert trailing commas."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4518
msgid "`ETC_Remove` (in configuration: `Remove`) Remove trailing commas."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4530
msgid ""
"**ExperimentalAutoDetectBinPacking** (`Boolean`) {versionbadge}`clang-format "
"3.7` {ref}`¶ <ExperimentalAutoDetectBinPacking>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4532
msgid ""
"If `true`, clang-format detects whether function calls and definitions are "
"formatted with one parameter per line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4535
msgid ""
"Each call can be bin-packed, one-per-line or inconclusive. If it is "
"inconclusive, e.g. completely on one line, but a decision needs to be made, "
"clang-format analyzes whether there are other bin-packed cases in the input "
"file and act accordingly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4541
msgid ""
"This is an experimental flag, that might go away or be renamed. Do not use "
"this in config files, etc. Use at your own risk."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4547
msgid ""
"**FixNamespaceComments** (`Boolean`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 5` {ref}`¶ "
"<FixNamespaceComments>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4549
msgid ""
"If `true`, clang-format adds missing namespace end comments for namespaces "
"and fixes invalid existing ones. This doesn't affect short namespaces, which "
"are controlled by `ShortNamespaceLines`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4566
msgid ""
"**ForEachMacros** (`List of Strings`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 3.7` {ref}"
"`¶ <ForEachMacros>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4568
msgid ""
"A vector of macros that should be interpreted as foreach loops instead of as "
"function calls."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4571
#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4593
#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5729
#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:8019
#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:8101
msgid "These are expected to be macros of the form:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4584
msgid "For example: BOOST_FOREACH."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4588
msgid ""
"**IfMacros** (`List of Strings`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 13` {ref}`¶ "
"<IfMacros>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4590
msgid ""
"A vector of macros that should be interpreted as conditionals instead of as "
"function calls."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4608
msgid ""
"For example: [KJ_IF_MAYBE](https://github.com/capnproto/capnproto/blob/"
"master/kjdoc/tour.md#maybes)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4613
msgid ""
"**IncludeBlocks** (`IncludeBlocksStyle`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 6` {ref}"
"`¶ <IncludeBlocks>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4615
msgid ""
"Dependent on the value, multiple `#include` blocks can be sorted as one and "
"divided based on category."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4620
msgid ""
"`IBS_Preserve` (in configuration: `Preserve`) Sort each `#include` block "
"separately."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4630
msgid ""
"`IBS_Merge` (in configuration: `Merge`) Merge multiple `#include` blocks "
"together and sort as one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4640
msgid ""
"`IBS_Regroup` (in configuration: `Regroup`) Merge multiple `#include` blocks "
"together and sort as one. Then split into groups based on category priority. "
"See `IncludeCategories`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4656
msgid ""
"**IncludeCategories** (`List of IncludeCategories`) {versionbadge}`clang-"
"format 3.8` {ref}`¶ <IncludeCategories>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4658
msgid ""
"Regular expressions denoting the different `#include` categories used for "
"ordering `#includes`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4661
msgid ""
"[POSIX extended](https://pubs.opengroup.org/onlinepubs/9699919799/basedefs/"
"V1_chap09.html) regular expressions are supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4665
msgid ""
"These regular expressions are matched against the filename of an include "
"(including the <> or \"\") in order. The value belonging to the first "
"matching regular expression is assigned and `#includes` are sorted first "
"according to increasing category number and then alphabetically within each "
"category."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4671
msgid ""
"If none of the regular expressions match, INT_MAX is assigned as category. "
"The main header for a source file automatically gets category 0. so that it "
"is generally kept at the beginning of the `#includes` (see [LLVM style]"
"(https://llvm.org/docs/CodingStandards.html#include-style)). However, you "
"can also assign negative priorities if you have certain headers that always "
"need to be first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4679
msgid ""
"There is a third and optional field `SortPriority` which can used while "
"`IncludeBlocks = IBS_Regroup` to define the priority in which `#includes` "
"should be ordered. The value of `Priority` defines the order of `#include "
"blocks` and also allows the grouping of `#includes` of different priority. "
"`SortPriority` is set to the value of `Priority` as default if it is not "
"assigned."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4686
msgid ""
"Each regular expression can be marked as case sensitive with the field "
"`CaseSensitive`, per default it is not."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4689
#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6473
msgid "To configure this in the .clang-format file, use:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4708
msgid ""
"**IncludeIsMainRegex** (`String`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 3.9` {ref}`¶ "
"<IncludeIsMainRegex>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4710
msgid ""
"Specify a regular expression of suffixes that are allowed in the file-to-"
"main-include mapping."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4713
msgid ""
"When guessing whether a #include is the \"main\" include (to assign category "
"0, see above), use this regex of allowed suffixes to the header stem. A "
"partial match is done, so that:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4716
msgid "`\"\"` means \"arbitrary suffix\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4717
msgid "`\"$\"` means \"no suffix\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4719
msgid ""
"For example, if configured to `\"(_test)?$\"`, then a header a.h would be "
"seen as the \"main\" include in both a.cc and a_test.cc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4724
msgid ""
"**IncludeIsMainSourceRegex** (`String`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 10` {ref}"
"`¶ <IncludeIsMainSourceRegex>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4726
msgid ""
"Specify a regular expression for files being formatted that are allowed to "
"be considered \"main\" in the file-to-main-include mapping."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4730
msgid ""
"By default, clang-format considers files as \"main\" only when they end "
"with: `.c`, `.cc`, `.cpp`, `.c++`, `.cxx`, `.m` or `.mm` extensions. For "
"these files a guessing of \"main\" include takes place (to assign category "
"0, see above). This config option allows for additional suffixes and "
"extensions for files to be considered as \"main\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4737
msgid ""
"For example, if this option is configured to `(Impl\\.hpp)$`, then a file "
"`ClassImpl.hpp` is considered \"main\" (in addition to `Class.c`, `Class."
"cc`, `Class.cpp` and so on) and \"main include file\" logic will be executed "
"(with *IncludeIsMainRegex* setting also being respected in later phase). "
"Without this option set, `ClassImpl.hpp` would not have the main include "
"file put on top before any other include."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4747
msgid ""
"**IndentAccessModifiers** (`Boolean`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 13` {ref}"
"`¶ <IndentAccessModifiers>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4749
msgid ""
"Specify whether access modifiers should have their own indentation level."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4751
msgid ""
"When `false`, access modifiers are indented (or outdented) relative to the "
"record members, respecting the `AccessModifierOffset`. Record members are "
"indented one level below the record. When `true`, access modifiers get their "
"own indentation level. As a consequence, record members are always indented "
"2 levels below the record, regardless of the access modifier presence. Value "
"of the `AccessModifierOffset` is ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4777
msgid ""
"**IndentCaseBlocks** (`Boolean`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 11` {ref}`¶ "
"<IndentCaseBlocks>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4779
msgid "Indent case label blocks one level from the case label."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4781
msgid ""
"When `false`, the block following the case label uses the same indentation "
"level as for the case label, treating the case label the same as an if-"
"statement. When `true`, the block gets indented as a scope block."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4803
msgid ""
"**IndentCaseLabels** (`Boolean`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 3.3` {ref}`¶ "
"<IndentCaseLabels>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4805
msgid "Indent case labels one level from the switch statement."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4807
msgid ""
"When `false`, use the same indentation level as for the switch statement. "
"Switch statement body is always indented one level more than case labels "
"(except the first block following the case label, which itself indents the "
"code - unless IndentCaseBlocks is enabled)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4825
msgid ""
"**IndentExportBlock** (`Boolean`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 20` {ref}`¶ "
"<IndentExportBlock>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4827
msgid ""
"If `true`, clang-format will indent the body of an `export { ... }` block. "
"This doesn't affect the formatting of anything else related to exported "
"declarations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4841
msgid ""
"**IndentExternBlock** (`IndentExternBlockStyle`) {versionbadge}`clang-format "
"11` {ref}`¶ <IndentExternBlock>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4843
msgid "IndentExternBlockStyle is the type of indenting of extern blocks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4847
msgid ""
"`IEBS_AfterExternBlock` (in configuration: `AfterExternBlock`) Backwards "
"compatible with AfterExternBlock's indenting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4867
msgid ""
"`IEBS_NoIndent` (in configuration: `NoIndent`) Does not indent extern blocks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4876
msgid "`IEBS_Indent` (in configuration: `Indent`) Indents extern blocks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4889
msgid ""
"**IndentGotoLabels** (`IndentGotoLabelStyle`) {versionbadge}`clang-format "
"10` {ref}`¶ <IndentGotoLabels>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4891
msgid "The goto label indenting style to use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4895
msgid ""
"`IGLS_NoIndent` (in configuration: `NoIndent`) Do not indent goto labels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4909
msgid ""
"`IGLS_OuterIndent` (in configuration: `OuterIndent`) Indent goto labels to "
"the enclosing block (previous indenting level)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4923
msgid ""
"`IGLS_InnerIndent` (in configuration: `InnerIndent`) Indent goto labels to "
"the surrounding statements (current indenting level)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4938
msgid ""
"`IGLS_HalfIndent` (in configuration: `HalfIndent`) Indent goto labels to "
"half the indentation of the surrounding code. If the indentation width is an "
"odd number, it will round up."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4957
msgid ""
"**IndentPPDirectives** (`PPDirectiveIndentStyle`) {versionbadge}`clang-"
"format 6` {ref}`¶ <IndentPPDirectives>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4959
msgid "The preprocessor directive indenting style to use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4963
msgid "`PPDIS_None` (in configuration: `None`) Does not indent any directives."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4974
msgid ""
"`PPDIS_AfterHash` (in configuration: `AfterHash`) Indents directives after "
"the hash."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4985
msgid ""
"`PPDIS_BeforeHash` (in configuration: `BeforeHash`) Indents directives "
"before the hash."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:4996
msgid ""
"`PPDIS_Leave` (in configuration: `Leave`) Leaves indentation of directives "
"as-is."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5000
msgid "Ignores `PPIndentWidth`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5015
msgid ""
"**IndentRequiresClause** (`Boolean`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 15` {ref}`¶ "
"<IndentRequiresClause>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5017
msgid ""
"Indent the requires clause in a template. This only applies when "
"`RequiresClausePosition` is `OwnLine`, `OwnLineWithBrace`, or "
"`WithFollowing`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5021
msgid "In clang-format 12, 13 and 14 it was named `IndentRequires`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5041
msgid ""
"**IndentWidth** (`Unsigned`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 3.7` {ref}`¶ "
"<IndentWidth>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5043
msgid "The number of columns to use for indentation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5058
msgid ""
"**IndentWrappedFunctionNames** (`Boolean`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 3.7` "
"{ref}`¶ <IndentWrappedFunctionNames>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5060
msgid ""
"Indent if a function definition or declaration is wrapped after the type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5075
msgid ""
"**InsertBraces** (`Boolean`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 15` {ref}`¶ "
"<InsertBraces>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5077
msgid ""
"Insert braces after control statements (`if`, `else`, `for`, `do`, and "
"`while`) in C++ unless the control statements are inside macro definitions "
"or the braces would enclose preprocessor directives."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5082
#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6582
#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6708
msgid ""
"Setting this option to `true` could lead to incorrect code formatting due to "
"clang-format's lack of complete semantic information. As such, extra care "
"should be taken to review code changes made by this option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5111
msgid ""
"**InsertNewlineAtEOF** (`Boolean`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 16` {ref}`¶ "
"<InsertNewlineAtEOF>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5113
msgid "Insert a newline at end of file if missing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5117
msgid ""
"**InsertTrailingCommas** (`TrailingCommaStyle`) {versionbadge}`clang-format "
"11` {ref}`¶ <InsertTrailingCommas>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5119
msgid ""
"If set to `TCS_Wrapped` will insert trailing commas in container literals "
"(arrays and objects) that wrap across multiple lines. It is currently only "
"available for JavaScript and disabled by default `TCS_None`. "
"`InsertTrailingCommas` cannot be used together with `BinPackArguments` as "
"inserting the comma disables bin-packing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5138
msgid "`TCS_None` (in configuration: `None`) Do not insert trailing commas."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5141
msgid ""
"`TCS_Wrapped` (in configuration: `Wrapped`) Insert trailing commas in "
"container literals that were wrapped over multiple lines. Note that this is "
"conceptually incompatible with bin-packing, because the trailing comma is "
"used as an indicator that a container should be formatted one-per-line (i.e. "
"not bin-packed). So inserting a trailing comma counteracts bin-packing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5152
msgid ""
"**IntegerLiteralSeparator** (`IntegerLiteralSeparatorStyle`) {versionbadge}"
"`clang-format 16` {ref}`¶ <IntegerLiteralSeparator>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5154
msgid ""
"Format integer literal separators (`'` for C/C++ and `_` for C#, Java, and "
"JavaScript)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5159
msgid "Separator format of integer literals of different bases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5161
msgid ""
"If negative, remove separators. If  `0`, leave the literal as is. If "
"positive, insert separators between digits starting from the rightmost digit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5165
msgid ""
"For example, the config below will leave separators in binary literals "
"alone, insert separators in decimal literals to separate the digits into "
"groups of 3, and remove separators in hexadecimal literals."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5176
msgid ""
"You can also specify a minimum number of digits (`BinaryMinDigitsInsert`, "
"`DecimalMinDigitsInsert`, and `HexMinDigitsInsert`) the integer literal must "
"have in order for the separators to be inserted, and a maximum number of "
"digits (`BinaryMaxDigitsRemove`, `DecimalMaxDigitsRemove`, and "
"`HexMaxDigitsRemove`) until the separators are removed. This divides the "
"literals in 3 regions, always without separator (up until including "
"`xxxMaxDigitsRemove`), maybe with, or without separators (up until excluding "
"`xxxMinDigitsInsert`), and finally always with separators."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5187
msgid ""
"`BinaryMinDigits`, `DecimalMinDigits`, and `HexMinDigits` are deprecated and "
"renamed to `BinaryMinDigitsInsert`, `DecimalMinDigitsInsert`, and "
"`HexMinDigitsInsert`, respectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5192
msgid "`int8_t Binary` Format separators in binary literals."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5201
msgid ""
"`int8_t BinaryMinDigitsInsert` Format separators in binary literals with a "
"minimum number of digits."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5210
msgid ""
"`int8_t BinaryMaxDigitsRemove` Remove separators in binary literals with a "
"maximum number of digits."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5223
msgid "`int8_t Decimal` Format separators in decimal literals."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5231
msgid ""
"`int8_t DecimalMinDigitsInsert` Format separators in decimal literals with a "
"minimum number of digits."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5240
msgid ""
"`int8_t DecimalMaxDigitsRemove` Remove separators in decimal literals with a "
"maximum number of digits."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5253
msgid "`int8_t Hex` Format separators in hexadecimal literals."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5261
msgid ""
"`int8_t HexMinDigitsInsert` Format separators in hexadecimal literals with a "
"minimum number of digits."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5271
msgid ""
"`int8_t HexMaxDigitsRemove` Remove separators in hexadecimal literals with a "
"maximum number of digits."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5288
msgid ""
"**JavaImportGroups** (`List of Strings`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 8` {ref}"
"`¶ <JavaImportGroups>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5290
msgid "A vector of prefixes ordered by the desired groups for Java imports."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5292
msgid ""
"One group's prefix can be a subset of another - the longest prefix is always "
"matched. Within a group, the imports are ordered lexicographically. Static "
"imports are grouped separately and follow the same group rules. By default, "
"static imports are placed before non-static imports, but this behavior is "
"changed by another option, `SortJavaStaticImport`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5299
msgid ""
"In the .clang-format configuration file, this can be configured like in the "
"following yaml example. This will result in imports being formatted as in "
"the Java example below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5325
msgid ""
"**JavaScriptQuotes** (`JavaScriptQuoteStyle`) {versionbadge}`clang-format "
"3.9` {ref}`¶ <JavaScriptQuotes>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5327
msgid "The JavaScriptQuoteStyle to use for JavaScript strings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5331
msgid ""
"`JSQS_Leave` (in configuration: `Leave`) Leave string quotes as they are."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5339
msgid "`JSQS_Single` (in configuration: `Single`) Always use single quotes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5347
msgid "`JSQS_Double` (in configuration: `Double`) Always use double quotes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5359
msgid ""
"**JavaScriptWrapImports** (`Boolean`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 3.9` {ref}"
"`¶ <JavaScriptWrapImports>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5361
msgid "Whether to wrap JavaScript import/export statements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5377
msgid ""
"**KeepEmptyLines** (`KeepEmptyLinesStyle`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 19` "
"{ref}`¶ <KeepEmptyLines>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5379
msgid ""
"Which empty lines are kept.  See `MaxEmptyLinesToKeep` for how many "
"consecutive empty lines are kept."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5384
msgid "Options regarding which empty lines are kept."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5386
msgid ""
"For example, the config below will remove empty lines at start of the file, "
"end of the file, and start of blocks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5396
msgid "`bool AtEndOfFile` Keep empty lines at end of file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5398
msgid "`bool AtStartOfBlock` Keep empty lines at start of a block."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5408
msgid "`bool AtStartOfFile` Keep empty lines at start of file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5413
msgid ""
"**KeepEmptyLinesAtEOF** (`Boolean`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 17` {ref}`¶ "
"<KeepEmptyLinesAtEOF>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5415
msgid "This option is **deprecated**. See `AtEndOfFile` of `KeepEmptyLines`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5419
msgid ""
"**KeepEmptyLinesAtTheStartOfBlocks** (`Boolean`) {versionbadge}`clang-format "
"3.7` {ref}`¶ <KeepEmptyLinesAtTheStartOfBlocks>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5421
msgid ""
"This option is **deprecated**. See `AtStartOfBlock` of `KeepEmptyLines`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5426
msgid ""
"**KeepFormFeed** (`Boolean`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 20` {ref}`¶ "
"<KeepFormFeed>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5428
msgid ""
"Keep the form feed character if it's immediately preceded and followed by a "
"newline. Multiple form feeds and newlines within a whitespace range are "
"replaced with a single newline and form feed followed by the remaining "
"newlines. (See www.gnu.org/prep/standards/html_node/Formatting.html#:~:"
"text=formfeed.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5436
msgid ""
"**LambdaBodyIndentation** (`LambdaBodyIndentationKind`) {versionbadge}`clang-"
"format 13` {ref}`¶ <LambdaBodyIndentation>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5438
msgid ""
"The indentation style of lambda bodies. `Signature` (the default) causes the "
"lambda body to be indented one additional level relative to the indentation "
"level of the signature. `OuterScope` forces the lambda body to be indented "
"one additional level relative to the parent scope containing the lambda "
"signature."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5446
msgid ""
"`LBI_Signature` (in configuration: `Signature`) Align lambda body relative "
"to the lambda signature. This is the default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5456
msgid ""
"`LBI_OuterScope` (in configuration: `OuterScope`) For statements within "
"block scope, align lambda body relative to the indentation level of the "
"outer scope the lambda signature resides in."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5476
msgid ""
"**Language** (`LanguageKind`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 3.5` {ref}`¶ "
"<Language>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5478
msgid "The language that this format style targets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5481
msgid ""
"You can specify the language (`C`, `Cpp`, or `ObjC`) for `.h` files by "
"adding a `// clang-format Language:` line before the first non-comment (and "
"non-empty) line, e.g. `// clang-format Language: Cpp`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5488
msgid "`LK_None` (in configuration: `None`) Do not use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5491
msgid "`LK_C` (in configuration: `C`) Should be used for C."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5494
msgid "`LK_Cpp` (in configuration: `Cpp`) Should be used for C++."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5497
msgid "`LK_CSharp` (in configuration: `CSharp`) Should be used for C#."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5500
msgid "`LK_Java` (in configuration: `Java`) Should be used for Java."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5503
msgid ""
"`LK_JavaScript` (in configuration: `JavaScript`) Should be used for "
"JavaScript."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5506
msgid "`LK_Json` (in configuration: `Json`) Should be used for JSON."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5509
msgid ""
"`LK_ObjC` (in configuration: `ObjC`) Should be used for Objective-C, "
"Objective-C++."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5512
msgid ""
"`LK_Proto` (in configuration: `Proto`) Should be used for [Protocol Buffers]"
"(https://protobuf.dev/)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5515
msgid ""
"`LK_TableGen` (in configuration: `TableGen`) Should be used for TableGen "
"code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5518
msgid ""
"`LK_TextProto` (in configuration: `TextProto`) Should be used for [Protocol "
"Buffer](https://protobuf.dev/) messages in text format"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5522
msgid ""
"`LK_Verilog` (in configuration: `Verilog`) Should be used for Verilog and "
"SystemVerilog. https://standards.ieee.org/ieee/1800/6700/ https://sci-hub."
"st/10.1109/IEEESTD.2018.8299595"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5531
msgid ""
"**LineEnding** (`LineEndingStyle`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 16` {ref}`¶ "
"<LineEnding>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5533
msgid "Line ending style (`\\n` or `\\r\\n`) to use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5537
msgid "`LE_LF` (in configuration: `LF`) Use `\\n`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5540
msgid "`LE_CRLF` (in configuration: `CRLF`) Use `\\r\\n`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5543
msgid ""
"`LE_DeriveLF` (in configuration: `DeriveLF`) Use `\\n` unless the input has "
"more lines ending in `\\r\\n`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5546
msgid ""
"`LE_DeriveCRLF` (in configuration: `DeriveCRLF`) Use `\\r\\n` unless the "
"input has more lines ending in `\\n`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5553
msgid ""
"**MacroBlockBegin** (`String`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 3.7` {ref}`¶ "
"<MacroBlockBegin>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5555
msgid "A regular expression matching macros that start a block."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5585
msgid ""
"**MacroBlockEnd** (`String`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 3.7` {ref}`¶ "
"<MacroBlockEnd>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5587
msgid "A regular expression matching macros that end a block."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5591
msgid ""
"**Macros** (`List of Strings`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 17` {ref}`¶ "
"<Macros>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5593
msgid "A list of macros of the form `<definition>=<expansion>` ."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5595
msgid ""
"Code will be parsed with macros expanded, in order to determine how to "
"interpret and format the macro arguments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5598
msgid "For example, the code:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5604
msgid ""
"will usually be interpreted as a call to a function A, and the "
"multiplication expression will be formatted as `a * b`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5607
msgid "If we specify the macro definition:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5614
msgid ""
"the code will now be parsed as a declaration of the variable b of type a*, "
"and formatted as `a* b` (depending on pointer-binding rules)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5617
msgid "Features and restrictions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5619
msgid "Both function-like macros and object-like macros are supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5620
msgid "Macro arguments must be used exactly once in the expansion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5621
msgid ""
"No recursive expansion; macros referencing other macros will be ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5623
msgid ""
"Overloading by arity is supported: for example, given the macro definitions "
"A=x, A()=y, A(a)=a"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5635
msgid ""
"**MacrosSkippedByRemoveParentheses** (`List of Strings`) {versionbadge}"
"`clang-format 21` {ref}`¶ <MacrosSkippedByRemoveParentheses>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5637
msgid ""
"A vector of function-like macros whose invocations should be skipped by "
"`RemoveParentheses`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5642
msgid ""
"**MainIncludeChar** (`MainIncludeCharDiscriminator`) {versionbadge}`clang-"
"format 19` {ref}`¶ <MainIncludeChar>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5644
msgid ""
"When guessing whether a #include is the \"main\" include, only the include "
"directives that use the specified character are considered."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5649
msgid ""
"`MICD_Quote` (in configuration: `Quote`) Main include uses quotes: `#include "
"\"foo.hpp\"` (the default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5652
msgid ""
"`MICD_AngleBracket` (in configuration: `AngleBracket`) Main include uses "
"angle brackets: `#include <foo.hpp>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5655
msgid ""
"`MICD_Any` (in configuration: `Any`) Main include uses either quotes or "
"angle brackets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5662
msgid ""
"**MaxEmptyLinesToKeep** (`Unsigned`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 3.7` {ref}"
"`¶ <MaxEmptyLinesToKeep>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5664
msgid "The maximum number of consecutive empty lines to keep."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5679
msgid ""
"**NamespaceIndentation** (`NamespaceIndentationKind`) {versionbadge}`clang-"
"format 3.7` {ref}`¶ <NamespaceIndentation>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5681
msgid "The indentation used for namespaces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5685
msgid "`NI_None` (in configuration: `None`) Don't indent in namespaces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5697
msgid ""
"`NI_Inner` (in configuration: `Inner`) Indent only in inner namespaces "
"(nested in other namespaces)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5709
msgid "`NI_All` (in configuration: `All`) Indent in all namespaces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5725
msgid ""
"**NamespaceMacros** (`List of Strings`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 9` {ref}"
"`¶ <NamespaceMacros>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5727
msgid "A vector of macros which are used to open namespace blocks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5737
msgid "For example: TESTSUITE"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5741
msgid ""
"**NumericLiteralCase** (`NumericLiteralCaseStyle`) {versionbadge}`clang-"
"format 22` {ref}`¶ <NumericLiteralCase>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5743
msgid "Capitalization style for numeric literals."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5747
msgid "Separate control for each numeric literal component."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5749
msgid ""
"For example, the config below will leave exponent letters alone, reformat "
"hexadecimal digits in lowercase, reformat numeric literal prefixes in "
"uppercase, and reformat suffixes in lowercase."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5761
msgid ""
"`NumericLiteralComponentStyle ExponentLetter` Format floating point exponent "
"separator letter case."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5772
#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5793
#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5814
#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5836
msgid ""
"`NLCS_Leave` (in configuration: `Leave`) Leave this component of the literal "
"as is."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5775
#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5796
#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5817
#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5839
msgid ""
"`NLCS_Upper` (in configuration: `Upper`) Format this component with "
"uppercase characters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5778
#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5799
#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5820
#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5842
msgid ""
"`NLCS_Lower` (in configuration: `Lower`) Format this component with "
"lowercase characters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5782
msgid "`NumericLiteralComponentStyle HexDigit` Format hexadecimal digit case."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5803
msgid "`NumericLiteralComponentStyle Prefix` Format integer prefix case."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5824
msgid ""
"`NumericLiteralComponentStyle Suffix` Format suffix case. This option "
"excludes case-sensitive reserved suffixes, such as `min` in C++."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5849
msgid ""
"**ObjCBinPackProtocolList** (`BinPackStyle`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 7` "
"{ref}`¶ <ObjCBinPackProtocolList>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5851
msgid ""
"Controls bin-packing Objective-C protocol conformance list items into as few "
"lines as possible when they go over `ColumnLimit`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5854
msgid ""
"If `Auto` (the default), delegates to the value in `BinPackParameters`. If "
"that is `BinPack`, bin-packs Objective-C protocol conformance list items "
"into as few lines as possible whenever they go over `ColumnLimit`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5859
msgid ""
"If `Always`, always bin-packs Objective-C protocol conformance list items "
"into as few lines as possible whenever they go over `ColumnLimit`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5863
msgid ""
"If `Never`, lays out Objective-C protocol conformance list items onto "
"individual lines whenever they go over `ColumnLimit`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5884
msgid ""
"`BPS_Auto` (in configuration: `Auto`) Automatically determine parameter bin-"
"packing behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5887
msgid "`BPS_Always` (in configuration: `Always`) Always bin-pack parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5890
msgid "`BPS_Never` (in configuration: `Never`) Never bin-pack parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5897
msgid ""
"**ObjCBlockIndentWidth** (`Unsigned`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 3.7` {ref}"
"`¶ <ObjCBlockIndentWidth>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5899
msgid "The number of characters to use for indentation of ObjC blocks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5911
msgid ""
"**ObjCBreakBeforeNestedBlockParam** (`Boolean`) {versionbadge}`clang-format "
"11` {ref}`¶ <ObjCBreakBeforeNestedBlockParam>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5913
msgid ""
"Break parameters list into lines when there is nested block parameters in a "
"function call."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5938
msgid ""
"**ObjCPropertyAttributeOrder** (`List of Strings`) {versionbadge}`clang-"
"format 18` {ref}`¶ <ObjCPropertyAttributeOrder>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5940
msgid "The order in which ObjC property attributes should appear."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5942
msgid ""
"Attributes in code will be sorted in the order specified. Any attributes "
"encountered that are not mentioned in this array will be sorted last, in "
"stable order. Comments between attributes will leave the attributes "
"untouched."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5948
msgid ""
"Using this option could lead to incorrect code formatting due to clang-"
"format's lack of complete semantic information. As such, extra care should "
"be taken to review code changes made by this option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5965
msgid ""
"**ObjCSpaceAfterMethodDeclarationPrefix** (`Boolean`) {versionbadge}`clang-"
"format 23` {ref}`¶ <ObjCSpaceAfterMethodDeclarationPrefix>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5967
msgid ""
"Add or remove a space between the '-'/'+' and the return type in Objective-C "
"method declarations. i.e"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5978
msgid ""
"**ObjCSpaceAfterProperty** (`Boolean`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 3.7` {ref}"
"`¶ <ObjCSpaceAfterProperty>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5980
msgid ""
"Add a space after `@property` in Objective-C, i.e. use `@property "
"(readonly)` instead of `@property(readonly)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5985
msgid ""
"**ObjCSpaceBeforeProtocolList** (`Boolean`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 3.7` "
"{ref}`¶ <ObjCSpaceBeforeProtocolList>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5987
msgid ""
"Add a space in front of an Objective-C protocol list, i.e. use `Foo "
"<Protocol>` instead of `Foo<Protocol>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5992
msgid ""
"**OneLineFormatOffRegex** (`String`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 21` {ref}`¶ "
"<OneLineFormatOffRegex>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:5994
msgid ""
"A regular expression that describes markers for turning formatting off for "
"one line. If it matches a comment that is the only token of a line, clang-"
"format skips the comment and the next line. Otherwise, clang-format skips "
"lines containing a matched token."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6000
msgid ""
"This option does not apply to `IntegerLiteralSeparator` and "
"`NumericLiteralCase`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6021
msgid ""
"**PPIndentWidth** (`Integer`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 13` {ref}`¶ "
"<PPIndentWidth>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6023
msgid ""
"The number of columns to use for indentation of preprocessor statements. "
"When set to -1 (default) `IndentWidth` is used also for preprocessor "
"statements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6039
msgid ""
"**PackArguments** (`PackArgumentsStyle`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 23` "
"{ref}`¶ <PackArguments>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6041
#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6045
msgid "Options related to packing arguments of function calls."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6047
msgid "`BinPackArgumentsStyle BinPack` {versionbadge}`clang-format 3.7`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6049
msgid "The bin pack arguments style to use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6053
msgid "`BPAS_BinPack` (in configuration: `BinPack`) Bin-pack arguments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6063
msgid ""
"`BPAS_OnePerLine` (in configuration: `OnePerLine`) Put all arguments on the "
"current line if they fit. Otherwise, put each one on its own line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6075
msgid ""
"`BPAS_UseBreakAfter` (in configuration: `UseBreakAfter`) Use the "
"`BreakAfter` option to handle argument packing instead. If the `BreakAfter` "
"limit is not exceeded, behave like `BinPack`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6080
msgid ""
"`unsigned BreakAfter` {versionbadge}`clang-format 23` An argument list with "
"more arguments than the specified number will be formatted with one argument "
"per line. This option must be used with `BinPack: UseBreakAfter`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6104
msgid ""
"**PackConstructorInitializers** (`PackConstructorInitializersStyle`) "
"{versionbadge}`clang-format 14` {ref}`¶ <PackConstructorInitializers>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6106
msgid "The pack constructor initializers style to use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6110
msgid ""
"`PCIS_Never` (in configuration: `Never`) Always put each constructor "
"initializer on its own line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6119
msgid ""
"`PCIS_BinPack` (in configuration: `BinPack`) Bin-pack constructor "
"initializers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6128
msgid ""
"`PCIS_CurrentLine` (in configuration: `CurrentLine`) Put all constructor "
"initializers on the current line if they fit. Otherwise, put each one on its "
"own line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6141
msgid ""
"`PCIS_NextLine` (in configuration: `NextLine`) Same as `PCIS_CurrentLine` "
"except that if all constructor initializers do not fit on the current line, "
"try to fit them on the next line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6157
msgid ""
"`PCIS_NextLineOnly` (in configuration: `NextLineOnly`) Put all constructor "
"initializers on the next line if they fit. Otherwise, put each one on its "
"own line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6178
msgid ""
"**PackParameters** (`PackParametersStyle`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 23` "
"{ref}`¶ <PackParameters>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6180
#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6185
msgid ""
"Options related to packing parameters of function declarations and "
"definitions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6188
msgid "`BinPackParametersStyle BinPack` {versionbadge}`clang-format 3.7`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6190
msgid "The bin pack parameters style to use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6228
msgid ""
"`unsigned BreakAfter` {versionbadge}`clang-format 23` A parameter list with "
"more parameters than the specified number will be formatted with one "
"parameter per line. This option must be used with `BinPack: UseBreakAfter`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6250
msgid ""
"**PenaltyBreakAssignment** (`Unsigned`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 5` {ref}"
"`¶ <PenaltyBreakAssignment>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6252
msgid "The penalty for breaking around an assignment operator."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6256
msgid ""
"**PenaltyBreakBeforeFirstCallParameter** (`Unsigned`) {versionbadge}`clang-"
"format 3.7` {ref}`¶ <PenaltyBreakBeforeFirstCallParameter>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6258
msgid "The penalty for breaking a function call after `call(`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6262
msgid ""
"**PenaltyBreakBeforeMemberAccess** (`Unsigned`) {versionbadge}`clang-format "
"20` {ref}`¶ <PenaltyBreakBeforeMemberAccess>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6264
msgid "The penalty for breaking before a member access operator (`.`, `->`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6268
msgid ""
"**PenaltyBreakComment** (`Unsigned`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 3.7` {ref}"
"`¶ <PenaltyBreakComment>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6270
msgid "The penalty for each line break introduced inside a comment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6274
msgid ""
