#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6280
msgid ""
"**PenaltyBreakOpenParenthesis** (`Unsigned`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 14` "
"{ref}`¶ <PenaltyBreakOpenParenthesis>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6282
msgid "The penalty for breaking after `(`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6286
msgid ""
"**PenaltyBreakScopeResolution** (`Unsigned`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 18` "
"{ref}`¶ <PenaltyBreakScopeResolution>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6288
msgid "The penalty for breaking after `::`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6292
msgid ""
"**PenaltyBreakString** (`Unsigned`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 3.7` {ref}`¶ "
"<PenaltyBreakString>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6294
msgid "The penalty for each line break introduced inside a string literal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6298
msgid ""
"**PenaltyBreakTemplateDeclaration** (`Unsigned`) {versionbadge}`clang-format "
"7` {ref}`¶ <PenaltyBreakTemplateDeclaration>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6300
msgid "The penalty for breaking after template declaration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6304
msgid ""
"**PenaltyExcessCharacter** (`Unsigned`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 3.7` "
"{ref}`¶ <PenaltyExcessCharacter>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6306
msgid "The penalty for each character outside of the column limit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6310
msgid ""
"**PenaltyIndentedWhitespace** (`Unsigned`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 12` "
"{ref}`¶ <PenaltyIndentedWhitespace>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6312
msgid ""
"Penalty for each character of whitespace indentation (counted relative to "
"leading non-whitespace column)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6317
msgid ""
"**PenaltyReturnTypeOnItsOwnLine** (`Unsigned`) {versionbadge}`clang-format "
"3.7` {ref}`¶ <PenaltyReturnTypeOnItsOwnLine>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6319
msgid "Penalty for putting the return type of a function onto its own line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6323
msgid ""
"**PointerAlignment** (`PointerAlignmentStyle`) {versionbadge}`clang-format "
"3.7` {ref}`¶ <PointerAlignment>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6325
msgid "Pointer and reference alignment style."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6329
msgid "`PAS_Left` (in configuration: `Left`) Align pointer to the left."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6336
msgid "`PAS_Right` (in configuration: `Right`) Align pointer to the right."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6343
msgid "`PAS_Middle` (in configuration: `Middle`) Align pointer in the middle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6354
msgid ""
"**QualifierAlignment** (`QualifierAlignmentStyle`) {versionbadge}`clang-"
"format 14` {ref}`¶ <QualifierAlignment>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6356
msgid ""
"Different ways to arrange specifiers and qualifiers (e.g. const/volatile)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6359
msgid ""
"Setting `QualifierAlignment`  to something other than `Leave`, COULD lead to "
"incorrect code formatting due to incorrect decisions made due to clang-"
"formats lack of complete semantic information. As such extra care should be "
"taken to review code changes made by the use of this option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6368
msgid ""
"`QAS_Leave` (in configuration: `Leave`) Don't change specifiers/qualifiers "
"to either Left or Right alignment (default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6377
msgid ""
"`QAS_Left` (in configuration: `Left`) Change specifiers/qualifiers to be "
"left-aligned."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6385
msgid ""
"`QAS_Right` (in configuration: `Right`) Change specifiers/qualifiers to be "
"right-aligned."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6393
msgid ""
"`QAS_Custom` (in configuration: `Custom`) Change specifiers/qualifiers to be "
"aligned based on `QualifierOrder`. With:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6411
msgid ""
"**QualifierOrder** (`List of Strings`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 14` {ref}"
"`¶ <QualifierOrder>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6413
msgid ""
"The order in which the qualifiers appear. The order is an array that can "
"contain any of the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6416
msgid "`const`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6417
msgid "`inline`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6418
msgid "`static`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6419
msgid "`friend`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6420
msgid "`constexpr`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6421
msgid "`volatile`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6422
msgid "`restrict`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6423
msgid "`typedef`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6424
msgid "`consteval`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6425
msgid "`constinit`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6426
msgid "`thread_local`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6427
msgid "`extern`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6428
msgid "`mutable`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6429
msgid "`signed`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6430
msgid "`unsigned`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6431
msgid "`long`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6432
msgid "`short`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6433
msgid "`explicit`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6434
msgid "`type`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6437
msgid "It must contain `type`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6440
msgid ""
"Items to the left of `type` will be placed to the left of the type and "
"aligned in the order supplied. Items to the right of `type` will be placed "
"to the right of the type and aligned in the order supplied. If only one of "
"`signed` and `unsigned` is specified, both are placed at that position. The "
"same applies to `long` and `short`. Specifying both members of a pair allows "
"them to be placed independently."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6453
msgid ""
"**RawStringFormats** (`List of RawStringFormats`) {versionbadge}`clang-"
"format 6` {ref}`¶ <RawStringFormats>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6455
msgid ""
"Defines hints for detecting supported languages code blocks in raw strings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6458
msgid ""
"A raw string with a matching delimiter or a matching enclosing function name "
"will be reformatted assuming the specified language based on the style for "
"that language defined in the .clang-format file. If no style has been "
"defined in the .clang-format file for the specific language, a predefined "
"style given by `BasedOnStyle` is used. If `BasedOnStyle` is not found, the "
"formatting is based on `LLVM` style. A matching delimiter takes precedence "
"over a matching enclosing function name for determining the language of the "
"raw string contents."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6467
msgid ""
"If a canonical delimiter is specified, occurrences of other delimiters for "
"the same language will be updated to the canonical if possible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6470
msgid ""
"There should be at most one specification per language and each delimiter "
"and enclosing function should not occur in multiple specifications."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6494
msgid ""
"**ReferenceAlignment** (`ReferenceAlignmentStyle`) {versionbadge}`clang-"
"format 13` {ref}`¶ <ReferenceAlignment>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6496
msgid ""
"Reference alignment style (overrides `PointerAlignment` for references)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6500
msgid ""
"`RAS_Pointer` (in configuration: `Pointer`) Align reference like "
"`PointerAlignment`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6503
msgid "`RAS_Left` (in configuration: `Left`) Align reference to the left."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6510
msgid "`RAS_Right` (in configuration: `Right`) Align reference to the right."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6517
msgid ""
"`RAS_Middle` (in configuration: `Middle`) Align reference in the middle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6528
msgid ""
"**ReflowComments** (`ReflowCommentsStyle`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 3.8` "
"{ref}`¶ <ReflowComments>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6530
msgid "Comment reformatting style."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6534
msgid "`RCS_Never` (in configuration: `Never`) Leave comments untouched."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6544
msgid ""
"`RCS_IndentOnly` (in configuration: `IndentOnly`) Only apply indentation "
"rules, moving comments left or right, without changing formatting inside the "
"comments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6555
msgid ""
"`RCS_Always` (in configuration: `Always`) Apply indentation rules and reflow "
"long comments into new lines, trying to obey the `ColumnLimit`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6572
msgid ""
"**RemoveBracesLLVM** (`Boolean`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 14` {ref}`¶ "
"<RemoveBracesLLVM>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6574
msgid ""
"Remove optional braces of control statements (`if`, `else`, `for`, and "
"`while`) in C++ according to the LLVM coding style."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6578
msgid "This option will be renamed and expanded to support other styles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6631
msgid ""
"**RemoveEmptyLinesInUnwrappedLines** (`Boolean`) {versionbadge}`clang-format "
"20` {ref}`¶ <RemoveEmptyLinesInUnwrappedLines>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6633
msgid "Remove empty lines within unwrapped lines."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6657
msgid ""
"**RemoveParentheses** (`RemoveParenthesesStyle`) {versionbadge}`clang-format "
"17` {ref}`¶ <RemoveParentheses>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6659
msgid "Remove redundant parentheses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6670
msgid "`RPS_Leave` (in configuration: `Leave`) Do not remove parentheses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6679
msgid ""
"`RPS_MultipleParentheses` (in configuration: `MultipleParentheses`) Replace "
"multiple parentheses with single parentheses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6688
msgid ""
"`RPS_ReturnStatement` (in configuration: `ReturnStatement`) Also remove "
"parentheses enclosing the expression in a `return`/`co_return` statement."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6702
msgid ""
"**RemoveSemicolon** (`Boolean`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 16` {ref}`¶ "
"<RemoveSemicolon>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6704
msgid ""
"Remove semicolons after the closing braces of functions and constructors/"
"destructors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6724
msgid ""
"**RequiresClausePosition** (`RequiresClausePositionStyle`) {versionbadge}"
"`clang-format 15` {ref}`¶ <RequiresClausePosition>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6726
msgid "The position of the `requires` clause."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6730
msgid ""
"`RCPS_OwnLine` (in configuration: `OwnLine`) Always put the `requires` "
"clause on its own line (possibly followed by a semicolon)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6753
msgid ""
"`RCPS_OwnLineWithBrace` (in configuration: `OwnLineWithBrace`) As with "
"`OwnLine`, except, unless otherwise prohibited, place a following open brace "
"(of a function definition) to follow on the same line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6773
msgid ""
"`RCPS_WithPreceding` (in configuration: `WithPreceding`) Try to put the "
"clause together with the preceding part of a declaration. For class "
"templates: stick to the template declaration. For function templates: stick "
"to the template declaration. For function declaration followed by a requires "
"clause: stick to the parameter list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6792
msgid ""
"`RCPS_WithFollowing` (in configuration: `WithFollowing`) Try to put the "
"`requires` clause together with the class or function declaration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6808
msgid ""
"`RCPS_SingleLine` (in configuration: `SingleLine`) Try to put everything in "
"the same line if possible. Otherwise normal line breaking rules take over."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6838
msgid ""
"**RequiresExpressionIndentation** (`RequiresExpressionIndentationKind`) "
"{versionbadge}`clang-format 16` {ref}`¶ <RequiresExpressionIndentation>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6840
msgid "The indentation used for requires expression bodies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6844
msgid ""
"`REI_OuterScope` (in configuration: `OuterScope`) Align requires expression "
"body relative to the indentation level of the outer scope the requires "
"expression resides in. This is the default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6856
msgid ""
"`REI_Keyword` (in configuration: `Keyword`) Align requires expression body "
"relative to the `requires` keyword."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6870
msgid ""
"**SeparateDefinitionBlocks** (`SeparateDefinitionStyle`) {versionbadge}"
"`clang-format 14` {ref}`¶ <SeparateDefinitionBlocks>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6872
msgid ""
"Specifies the use of empty lines to separate definition blocks, including "
"classes, structs, enums, and functions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6921
msgid ""
"`SDS_Leave` (in configuration: `Leave`) Leave definition blocks as they are."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6924
msgid ""
"`SDS_Always` (in configuration: `Always`) Insert an empty line between "
"definition blocks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6927
msgid ""
"`SDS_Never` (in configuration: `Never`) Remove any empty line between "
"definition blocks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6934
msgid ""
"**ShortNamespaceLines** (`Unsigned`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 13` {ref}`¶ "
"<ShortNamespaceLines>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6936
msgid ""
"The maximal number of unwrapped lines that a short namespace spans. Defaults "
"to 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6939
msgid ""
"This determines the maximum length of short namespaces by counting unwrapped "
"lines (i.e. containing neither opening nor closing namespace brace) and "
"makes `FixNamespaceComments` omit adding end comments for those."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6959
msgid ""
"**SkipMacroDefinitionBody** (`Boolean`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 18` {ref}"
"`¶ <SkipMacroDefinitionBody>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6961
msgid "Do not format macro definition body."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6965
msgid ""
"**SortIncludes** (`SortIncludesOptions`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 3.8` "
"{ref}`¶ <SortIncludes>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6967
msgid "Controls if and how clang-format will sort `#includes`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6971
msgid "Includes sorting options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6973
msgid ""
"`bool Enabled` If `true`, includes are sorted based on the other suboptions "
"below. (`Never` is deprecated by `Enabled: false`.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6976
msgid ""
"`bool IgnoreCase` Whether or not includes are sorted in a case-insensitive "
"fashion. (`CaseSensitive` and `CaseInsensitive` are deprecated by "
"`IgnoreCase: false` and `IgnoreCase: true`, respectively.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6989
msgid ""
"`bool IgnoreExtension` When sorting includes in each block, only take file "
"extensions into account if two includes compare equal otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:6999
msgid ""
"`bool Natural` Whether or not includes are sorted by natural ordering i.e., "
"whether embedded runs of digits are compared as numbers rather than "
"sequences of characters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7012
msgid ""
"**SortJavaStaticImport** (`SortJavaStaticImportOptions`) {versionbadge}"
"`clang-format 12` {ref}`¶ <SortJavaStaticImport>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7014
msgid ""
"When sorting Java imports, by default static imports are placed before non-"
"static imports. If `JavaStaticImportAfterImport` is `After`, static imports "
"are placed after non-static imports."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7020
msgid ""
"`SJSIO_Before` (in configuration: `Before`) Static imports are placed before "
"non-static imports."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7029
msgid ""
"`SJSIO_After` (in configuration: `After`) Static imports are placed after "
"non-static imports."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7042
msgid ""
"**SortUsingDeclarations** (`SortUsingDeclarationsOptions`) {versionbadge}"
"`clang-format 5` {ref}`¶ <SortUsingDeclarations>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7044
msgid "Controls if and how clang-format will sort using declarations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7048
msgid ""
"`SUD_Never` (in configuration: `Never`) Using declarations are never sorted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7059
msgid ""
"`SUD_Lexicographic` (in configuration: `Lexicographic`) Using declarations "
"are sorted in the order defined as follows: Split the strings by `::` and "
"discard any initial empty strings. Sort the lists of names "
"lexicographically, and within those groups, names are in case-insensitive "
"lexicographic order."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7073
msgid ""
"`SUD_LexicographicNumeric` (in configuration: `LexicographicNumeric`) Using "
"declarations are sorted in the order defined as follows: Split the strings "
"by `::` and discard any initial empty strings. The last element of each list "
"is a non-namespace name; all others are namespace names. Sort the lists of "
"names lexicographically, where the sort order of individual names is that "
"all non-namespace names come before all namespace names, and within those "
"groups, names are in case-insensitive lexicographic order."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7094
msgid ""
"**SpaceAfterCStyleCast** (`Boolean`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 3.5` {ref}"
"`¶ <SpaceAfterCStyleCast>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7096
msgid "If `true`, a space is inserted after C style casts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7105
msgid ""
"**SpaceAfterLogicalNot** (`Boolean`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 9` {ref}`¶ "
"<SpaceAfterLogicalNot>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7107
msgid "If `true`, a space is inserted after the logical not operator (`!`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7116
msgid ""
"**SpaceAfterOperatorKeyword** (`Boolean`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 21` "
"{ref}`¶ <SpaceAfterOperatorKeyword>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7118
msgid "If `true`, a space will be inserted after the `operator` keyword."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7127
msgid ""
"**SpaceAfterTemplateKeyword** (`Boolean`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 4` "
"{ref}`¶ <SpaceAfterTemplateKeyword>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7129
msgid "If `true`, a space will be inserted after the `template` keyword."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7138
msgid ""
"**SpaceAroundPointerQualifiers** (`SpaceAroundPointerQualifiersStyle`) "
"{versionbadge}`clang-format 12` {ref}`¶ <SpaceAroundPointerQualifiers>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7140
msgid ""
"Defines in which cases to put a space before or after pointer qualifiers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7144
msgid ""
"`SAPQ_Default` (in configuration: `Default`) Don't ensure spaces around "
"pointer qualifiers and use PointerAlignment instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7153
msgid ""
"`SAPQ_Before` (in configuration: `Before`) Ensure that there is a space "
"before pointer qualifiers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7161
msgid ""
"`SAPQ_After` (in configuration: `After`) Ensure that there is a space after "
"pointer qualifiers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7169
msgid ""
"`SAPQ_Both` (in configuration: `Both`) Ensure that there is a space both "
"before and after pointer qualifiers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7181
msgid ""
"**SpaceBeforeAssignmentOperators** (`Boolean`) {versionbadge}`clang-format "
"3.7` {ref}`¶ <SpaceBeforeAssignmentOperators>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7183
msgid "If `false`, spaces will be removed before assignment operators."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7193
msgid ""
"**SpaceBeforeCaseColon** (`Boolean`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 12` {ref}`¶ "
"<SpaceBeforeCaseColon>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7195
msgid "If `false`, spaces will be removed before case colon."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7206
msgid ""
"**SpaceBeforeCpp11BracedList** (`Boolean`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 7` "
"{ref}`¶ <SpaceBeforeCpp11BracedList>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7208
msgid ""
"If `true`, a space will be inserted before a C++11 braced list used to "
"initialize an object (after the preceding identifier or type)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7221
msgid ""
"**SpaceBeforeCtorInitializerColon** (`Boolean`) {versionbadge}`clang-format "
"7` {ref}`¶ <SpaceBeforeCtorInitializerColon>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7223
msgid ""
"If `false`, spaces will be removed before constructor initializer colon."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7233
msgid ""
"**SpaceBeforeEnumUnderlyingTypeColon** (`Boolean`) {versionbadge}`clang-"
"format 23` {ref}`¶ <SpaceBeforeEnumUnderlyingTypeColon>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7235
msgid "If `false`, spaces will be removed before enum underlying type colon."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7244
msgid ""
"**SpaceBeforeInheritanceColon** (`Boolean`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 7` "
"{ref}`¶ <SpaceBeforeInheritanceColon>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7246
msgid "If `false`, spaces will be removed before inheritance colon."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7255
msgid ""
"**SpaceBeforeJsonColon** (`Boolean`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 17` {ref}`¶ "
"<SpaceBeforeJsonColon>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7257
msgid ""
"If `true`, a space will be added before a JSON colon. For other languages, e."
"g. JavaScript, use `SpacesInContainerLiterals` instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7269
msgid ""
"**SpaceBeforeParens** (`SpaceBeforeParensStyle`) {versionbadge}`clang-format "
"3.5` {ref}`¶ <SpaceBeforeParens>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7271
msgid "Defines in which cases to put a space before opening parentheses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7275
msgid ""
"`SBPO_Never` (in configuration: `Never`) This is **deprecated** and replaced "
"by `Custom` below, with all `SpaceBeforeParensOptions` but "
"`AfterPlacementOperator` set to `false`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7280
msgid ""
"`SBPO_ControlStatements` (in configuration: `ControlStatements`) Put a space "
"before opening parentheses only after control statement keywords (`for/if/"
"while...`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7292
msgid ""
"`SBPO_ControlStatementsExceptControlMacros` (in configuration: "
"`ControlStatementsExceptControlMacros`) Same as `SBPO_ControlStatements` "
"except this option doesn't apply to ForEach and If macros. This is useful in "
"projects where ForEach/If macros are treated as function calls instead of "
"control statements. `SBPO_ControlStatementsExceptForEachMacros` remains an "
"alias for backward compatibility."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7307
msgid ""
"`SBPO_NonEmptyParentheses` (in configuration: `NonEmptyParentheses`) Put a "
"space before opening parentheses only if the parentheses are not empty."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7320
msgid ""
"`SBPO_Always` (in configuration: `Always`) Always put a space before opening "
"parentheses, except when it's prohibited by the syntax rules (in function-"
"like macro definitions) or when determined by other style rules (after unary "
"operators, opening parentheses, etc.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7334
msgid ""
"`SBPO_Custom` (in configuration: `Custom`) Configure each individual space "
"before parentheses in `SpaceBeforeParensOptions`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7342
msgid ""
"**SpaceBeforeParensOptions** (`SpaceBeforeParensCustom`) {versionbadge}"
"`clang-format 14` {ref}`¶ <SpaceBeforeParensOptions>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7344
msgid "Control of individual space before parentheses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7346
msgid ""
"If `SpaceBeforeParens` is set to `Custom`, use this to specify how each "
"individual space before parentheses case should be handled. Otherwise, this "
"is ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7360
msgid "Precise control over the spacing before parentheses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7370
msgid ""
"`bool AfterControlStatements` If `true`, put space between control statement "
"keywords (for/if/while...) and opening parentheses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7378
msgid ""
"`bool AfterForeachMacros` If `true`, put space between foreach macros and "
"opening parentheses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7386
msgid ""
"`bool AfterFunctionDeclarationName` If `true`, put a space between function "
"declaration name and opening parentheses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7394
msgid ""
"`bool AfterFunctionDefinitionName` If `true`, put a space between function "
"definition name and opening parentheses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7402
msgid ""
"`bool AfterIfMacros` If `true`, put space between if macros and opening "
"parentheses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7410
msgid ""
"`bool AfterNot` If `true`, put a space between alternative operator `not` "
"and the opening parenthesis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7418
msgid ""
"`bool AfterOverloadedOperator` If `true`, put a space between operator "
"overloading and opening parentheses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7427
msgid ""
"`bool AfterPlacementOperator` If `true`, put a space between operator `new`/"
"`delete` and opening parenthesis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7436
msgid ""
"`bool AfterRequiresInClause` If `true`, put space between requires keyword "
"in a requires clause and opening parentheses, if there is one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7446
msgid ""
"`bool AfterRequiresInExpression` If `true`, put space between requires "
"keyword in a requires expression and opening parentheses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7457
msgid ""
"`bool BeforeNonEmptyParentheses` If `true`, put a space before opening "
"parentheses only if the parentheses are not empty."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7469
msgid ""
"**SpaceBeforeRangeBasedForLoopColon** (`Boolean`) {versionbadge}`clang-"
"format 7` {ref}`¶ <SpaceBeforeRangeBasedForLoopColon>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7471
msgid "If `false`, spaces will be removed before range-based for loop colon."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7481
msgid ""
"**SpaceBeforeSquareBrackets** (`Boolean`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 10` "
"{ref}`¶ <SpaceBeforeSquareBrackets>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7483
msgid ""
"If `true`, spaces will be before  `[`. Lambdas will not be affected. Only "
"the first `[` will get a space added."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7494
msgid ""
"**SpaceInEmptyBlock** (`Boolean`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 10` {ref}`¶ "
"<SpaceInEmptyBlock>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7496
msgid "This option is **deprecated**. See `Block` of `SpaceInEmptyBraces`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7500
msgid ""
"**SpaceInEmptyBraces** (`SpaceInEmptyBracesStyle`) {versionbadge}`clang-"
"format 22` {ref}`¶ <SpaceInEmptyBraces>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7502
msgid "Specifies when to insert a space in empty braces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7505
msgid ""
"This option doesn't apply to initializer braces if `Cpp11BracedListStyle` is "
"not `Block`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7511
msgid ""
"`SIEB_Always` (in configuration: `Always`) Always insert a space in empty "
"braces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7521
msgid ""
"`SIEB_Block` (in configuration: `Block`) Only insert a space in empty blocks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7531
msgid ""
"`SIEB_Never` (in configuration: `Never`) Never insert a space in empty "
"braces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7545
msgid ""
"**SpaceInEmptyParentheses** (`Boolean`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 3.7` "
"{ref}`¶ <SpaceInEmptyParentheses>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7547
msgid ""
"If `true`, spaces may be inserted into `()`. This option is **deprecated**. "
"See `InEmptyParentheses` of `SpacesInParensOptions`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7553
msgid ""
"**SpacesBeforeTrailingComments** (`Unsigned`) {versionbadge}`clang-format "
"3.7` {ref}`¶ <SpacesBeforeTrailingComments>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7555
msgid "The number of spaces before trailing line comments (`//` - comments)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7558
msgid ""
"This does not affect trailing block comments (`/*` - comments) as those "
"commonly have different usage patterns and a number of special cases.  In "
"the case of Verilog, it doesn't affect a comment right after the opening "
"parenthesis in the port or parameter list in a module header, because it is "
"probably for the port on the following line instead of the parenthesis it "
"follows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7576
msgid ""
"**SpacesInAngles** (`SpacesInAnglesStyle`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 3.4` "
"{ref}`¶ <SpacesInAngles>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7578
msgid "The SpacesInAnglesStyle to use for template argument lists."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7582
msgid ""
"`SIAS_Never` (in configuration: `Never`) Remove spaces after `<` and before "
"`>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7590
msgid ""
"`SIAS_Always` (in configuration: `Always`) Add spaces after `<` and before "
"`>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7598
msgid ""
"`SIAS_Leave` (in configuration: `Leave`) Keep a single space after `<` and "
"before `>` if any spaces were present. Option `Standard: Cpp03` takes "
"precedence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7606
msgid ""
"**SpacesInBlockComments** (`SpacesInBlockCommentsStyle`) {versionbadge}"
"`clang-format 24` {ref}`¶ <SpacesInBlockComments>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7608
msgid ""
"The SpacesInBlockCommentsStyle to use for ordinary block comments. "
"Documentation comments such as `/** ... */` and `/*! ... */` and parameter "
"comments ending with `=` before the closing `*/` are left unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7615
msgid ""
"`SIBCS_Never` (in configuration: `Never`) Remove spaces after `/*` and "
"before `*/`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7622
msgid ""
"`SIBCS_Always` (in configuration: `Always`) Add spaces after `/*` and before "
"`*/`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7629
msgid ""
"`SIBCS_Leave` (in configuration: `Leave`) Leave existing spaces unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7636
msgid ""
"**SpacesInCStyleCastParentheses** (`Boolean`) {versionbadge}`clang-format "
"3.7` {ref}`¶ <SpacesInCStyleCastParentheses>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7638
msgid ""
"If `true`, spaces may be inserted into C style casts. This option is "
"**deprecated**. See `InCStyleCasts` of `SpacesInParensOptions`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7644
msgid ""
"**SpacesInConditionalStatement** (`Boolean`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 10` "
"{ref}`¶ <SpacesInConditionalStatement>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7646
msgid ""
"If `true`, spaces will be inserted around if/for/switch/while conditions. "
"This option is **deprecated**. See `InConditionalStatements` of "
"`SpacesInParensOptions`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7653
msgid ""
"**SpacesInContainerLiterals** (`Boolean`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 3.7` "
"{ref}`¶ <SpacesInContainerLiterals>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7655
msgid ""
"If `true`, spaces are inserted inside container literals (e.g.  ObjC and "
"Javascript array and dict literals). For JSON, use `SpaceBeforeJsonColon` "
"instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7667
msgid ""
"**SpacesInLineCommentPrefix** (`SpacesInLineComment`) {versionbadge}`clang-"
"format 13` {ref}`¶ <SpacesInLineCommentPrefix>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7669
msgid ""
"How many spaces are allowed at the start of a line comment. To disable the "
"maximum set it to `-1`, apart from that the maximum takes precedence over "
"the minimum."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7685
msgid ""
"Note that in line comment sections the relative indent of the subsequent "
"lines is kept, that means the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7701
msgid "This option has only effect if `ReflowComments` is set to `true`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7705
msgid "Control of spaces within a single line comment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7707
msgid ""
"`unsigned Minimum` The minimum number of spaces at the start of the comment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7709
msgid ""
"`unsigned Maximum` The maximum number of spaces at the start of the comment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7714
msgid ""
"**SpacesInParens** (`SpacesInParensStyle`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 17` "
"{ref}`¶ <SpacesInParens>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7716
msgid ""
"Defines in which cases spaces will be inserted after `(` and before `)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7721
msgid ""
"`SIPO_Never` (in configuration: `Never`) Never put a space in parentheses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7732
msgid ""
"`SIPO_Custom` (in configuration: `Custom`) Configure each individual space "
"in parentheses in `SpacesInParensOptions`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7740
msgid ""
"**SpacesInParensOptions** (`SpacesInParensCustom`) {versionbadge}`clang-"
"format 17` {ref}`¶ <SpacesInParensOptions>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7742
msgid "Control of individual spaces in parentheses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7744
msgid ""
"If `SpacesInParens` is set to `Custom`, use this to specify how each "
"individual space in parentheses case should be handled. Otherwise, this is "
"ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7759
msgid "Precise control over the spacing in parentheses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7770
msgid ""
"`bool ExceptDoubleParentheses` Override any of the following options to "
"prevent addition of space when both opening and closing parentheses use "
"multiple parentheses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7783
msgid ""
"`bool InConditionalStatements` Put a space in parentheses only inside "
"conditional statements (`for/if/while/switch...`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7792
msgid "`bool InCStyleCasts` Put a space in C style casts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7800
msgid ""
"`bool InEmptyParentheses` Insert a space in empty parentheses, i.e. `()`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7812
msgid ""
"`bool Other` Put a space in parentheses not covered by preceding options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7822
msgid ""
"**SpacesInParentheses** (`Boolean`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 3.7` {ref}`¶ "
"<SpacesInParentheses>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7824
msgid ""
"If `true`, spaces will be inserted after `(` and before `)`. This option is "
"**deprecated**. The previous behavior is preserved by using `SpacesInParens` "
"with `Custom` and by setting all `SpacesInParensOptions` to `true` except "
"for `InCStyleCasts` and `InEmptyParentheses`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7832
msgid ""
"**SpacesInSquareBrackets** (`Boolean`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 3.7` {ref}"
"`¶ <SpacesInSquareBrackets>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7834
msgid ""
"If `true`, spaces will be inserted after `[` and before `]`. Lambdas without "
"arguments or unspecified size array declarations will not be affected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7846
msgid ""
"**Standard** (`LanguageStandard`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 3.7` {ref}`¶ "
"<Standard>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7848
msgid "Parse and format C++ constructs compatible with this standard."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7857
msgid ""
"`LS_Cpp03` (in configuration: `c++03`) Parse and format as C++03. `Cpp03` is "
"a deprecated alias for `c++03`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7861
msgid "`LS_Cpp11` (in configuration: `c++11`) Parse and format as C++11."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7864
msgid "`LS_Cpp14` (in configuration: `c++14`) Parse and format as C++14."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7867
msgid "`LS_Cpp17` (in configuration: `c++17`) Parse and format as C++17."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7870
msgid "`LS_Cpp20` (in configuration: `c++20`) Parse and format as C++20."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7873
msgid "`LS_Cpp23` (in configuration: `c++23`) Parse and format as C++23."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7876
msgid "`LS_Cpp26` (in configuration: `c++26`) Parse and format as C++26."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7879
msgid ""
"`LS_Latest` (in configuration: `Latest`) Parse and format using the latest "
"supported language version. `Cpp11` is a deprecated alias for `Latest`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7883
msgid ""
"`LS_Auto` (in configuration: `Auto`) Automatic detection based on the input."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7890
msgid ""
"**StatementAttributeLikeMacros** (`List of Strings`) {versionbadge}`clang-"
"format 12` {ref}`¶ <StatementAttributeLikeMacros>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7892
msgid ""
"Macros which are ignored in front of a statement, as if they were an "
"attribute. So that they are not parsed as identifier, for example for Qts "
"emit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7910
msgid ""
"**StatementMacros** (`List of Strings`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 8` {ref}"
"`¶ <StatementMacros>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7912
msgid "A vector of macros that should be interpreted as complete statements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7914
msgid ""
"Typical macros are expressions and require a semicolon to be added. "
"Sometimes this is not the case, and this allows to make clang-format aware "
"of such cases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7918
msgid "For example: Q_UNUSED"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7922
msgid ""
"**TabWidth** (`Unsigned`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 3.7` {ref}`¶ "
"<TabWidth>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7924
msgid "The number of columns used for tab stops."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7928
msgid ""
"**TableGenBreakInsideDAGArg** (`DAGArgStyle`) {versionbadge}`clang-format "
"19` {ref}`¶ <TableGenBreakInsideDAGArg>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7930
msgid "The styles of the line break inside the DAGArg in TableGen."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7934
msgid ""
"`DAS_DontBreak` (in configuration: `DontBreak`) Never break inside DAGArg."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7941
msgid ""
"`DAS_BreakElements` (in configuration: `BreakElements`) Break inside DAGArg "
"after each list element but for the last. This aligns to the first element."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7950
msgid ""
"`DAS_BreakAll` (in configuration: `BreakAll`) Break inside DAGArg after the "
"operator and the all elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7964
msgid ""
"**TableGenBreakingDAGArgOperators** (`List of Strings`) {versionbadge}`clang-"
"format 19` {ref}`¶ <TableGenBreakingDAGArgOperators>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7966
msgid ""
"Works only when TableGenBreakInsideDAGArg is not DontBreak. The string list "
"needs to consist of identifiers in TableGen. If any identifier is specified, "
"this limits the line breaks by TableGenBreakInsideDAGArg option only on "
"DAGArg values beginning with the specified identifiers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7972
msgid "For example the configuration,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7979
msgid ""
"makes the line break only occurs inside DAGArgs beginning with the specified "
"identifiers `ins` and `outs`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7993
msgid ""
"**TemplateNames** (`List of Strings`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 20` {ref}"
"`¶ <TemplateNames>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7995
msgid ""
"A vector of non-keyword identifiers that should be interpreted as template "
"names."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:7998
msgid ""
"A `<` after a template name is annotated as a template opener instead of a "
"binary operator."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:8003
msgid ""
"**TypeNames** (`List of Strings`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 17` {ref}`¶ "
"<TypeNames>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:8005
msgid ""
"A vector of non-keyword identifiers that should be interpreted as type names."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:8008
msgid ""
"A `*`, `&`, or `&&` between a type name and another non-keyword identifier "
"is annotated as a pointer or reference token instead of a binary operator."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:8014
msgid ""
"**TypenameMacros** (`List of Strings`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 9` {ref}"
"`¶ <TypenameMacros>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:8016
msgid ""
"A vector of macros that should be interpreted as type declarations instead "
"of as function calls."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:8031
msgid "For example: OpenSSL STACK_OF, BSD LIST_ENTRY."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:8035
msgid ""
"**UseCRLF** (`Boolean`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 10` {ref}`¶ <UseCRLF>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:8037
msgid "This option is **deprecated**. See `LF` and `CRLF` of `LineEnding`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:8041
msgid ""
"**UseTab** (`UseTabStyle`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 3.7` {ref}`¶ <UseTab>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:8043
msgid "The way to use tab characters in the resulting file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:8047
msgid "`UT_Never` (in configuration: `Never`) Never use tab."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:8050
msgid ""
"`UT_ForIndentation` (in configuration: `ForIndentation`) Use tabs only for "
"indentation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:8053
msgid ""
"`UT_ForContinuationAndIndentation` (in configuration: "
"`ForContinuationAndIndentation`) Fill all leading whitespace with tabs, and "
"use spaces for alignment that appears within a line (e.g. consecutive "
"assignments and declarations)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:8057
msgid ""
"`UT_AlignWithSpaces` (in configuration: `AlignWithSpaces`) Use tabs for line "
"continuation and indentation, and spaces for alignment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:8061
msgid ""
"`UT_Always` (in configuration: `Always`) Use tabs whenever we need to fill "
"whitespace that spans at least from one tab stop to the next one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:8069
msgid ""
"**VariableTemplates** (`List of Strings`) {versionbadge}`clang-format 20` "
"{ref}`¶ <VariableTemplates>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:8071
msgid ""
"A vector of non-keyword identifiers that should be interpreted as variable "
"template names."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:8074
msgid ""
"A `)` after a variable template instantiation is **not** annotated as the "
"closing parenthesis of C-style cast operator."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:8079
msgid ""
"**VerilogBreakBetweenInstancePorts** (`Boolean`) {versionbadge}`clang-format "
"17` {ref}`¶ <VerilogBreakBetweenInstancePorts>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:8081
msgid "For Verilog, put each port on its own line in module instantiations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:8096
msgid ""
"**WhitespaceSensitiveMacros** (`List of Strings`) {versionbadge}`clang-"
"format 11` {ref}`¶ <WhitespaceSensitiveMacros>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:8098
msgid ""
"A vector of macros which are whitespace-sensitive and should not be touched."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:8113
msgid "For example: BOOST_PP_STRINGIZE"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:8117
msgid ""
"**WrapNamespaceBodyWithEmptyLines** (`WrapNamespaceBodyWithEmptyLinesStyle`) "
"{versionbadge}`clang-format 20` {ref}`¶ <WrapNamespaceBodyWithEmptyLines>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:8119
msgid "Wrap namespace body with empty lines."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:8123
msgid ""
"`WNBWELS_Never` (in configuration: `Never`) Remove all empty lines at the "
"beginning and the end of namespace body."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:8134
msgid ""
"`WNBWELS_Always` (in configuration: `Always`) Always have at least one empty "
"line at the beginning and the end of namespace body except that the number "
"of empty lines between consecutive nested namespace definitions is not "
"increased."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:8149
msgid ""
"`WNBWELS_Leave` (in configuration: `Leave`) Keep existing newlines at the "
"beginning and the end of namespace body. `MaxEmptyLinesToKeep` still applies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:8157
msgid "Adding additional style options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:8159
msgid ""
"Each additional style option adds costs to the clang-format project. Some of "
"these costs affect the clang-format development itself, as we need to make "
"sure that any given combination of options work and that new features don't "
"break any of the existing options in any way. There are also costs for end "
"users as options become less discoverable and people have to think about and "
"make a decision on options they don't really care about."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:8166
msgid ""
"The goal of the clang-format project is more on the side of supporting a "
"limited set of styles really well as opposed to supporting every single "
"style used by a codebase somewhere in the wild. Of course, we do want to "
"support all major projects and thus have established the following bar for "
"adding style options. Each new style option must:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:8172
msgid "be used in a project of significant size (have dozens of contributors)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:8173
msgid "have a publicly accessible style guide"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:8174
msgid "have a person willing to contribute and maintain patches"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ClangFormatStyleOptions.md:8176
msgid "Examples"
msgstr ""

